# Entity Layer Architecture

Two entity types, in separate projects:

| Layer | Project | Purpose |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Domain entities | `NTierTemplate/` | Rich domain models with business logic; used in domain services |
| EF entities | `NTierTemplate.Data/` | Persistence models mapping to tables/columns; used only in repositories and DbContext |

## Rules

- **Domain services** (`UserService`, etc.) live in `NTierTemplate/`; they use domain types and repository interfaces only
- When investigating database issues or schema: look at EF entities in `NTierTemplate.Data`, not domain entities
- When writing LINQ queries or EF Core code: reference EF entities in `NTierTemplate.Data`
- Repositories translate between EF entities and domain entities at CRUD and query level
- ASP.NET Core Identity persistence types (`ApplicationUser`, `ApplicationRole`) live in `NTierTemplate.Data`; map to domain `User` in repositories
- Identity managers (`UserManager`, `RoleManager`) are used inside repository implementations in `NTierTemplate.Data`, not in domain services, Api controllers, or Cli handlers
- Api and Cli depend on domain services (`IUserService`, etc.), not repository interfaces or Identity types

